      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight you carry is real, but the \"quietness\" you fear might actually be the heavy silence of letting go rather than the peace of freedom. While the shame feels universal, it is a prison you are building for yourself; true meaning often finds itself only when we stop fighting circumstances we cannot control and start focusing on what remains. You deserve to breathe without the constant pressure to perform, even if the journey there feels slow and uncertain.",
      "source": "target",
